{
  "description": "Language-agnostic laws of the analysis.check geometry widgets. Shapes are the recipes of the analysis.measure fixture; a mesh is a recipe with explicit positions and polygon faces (indices wound counter-clockwise seen from outside). A validity report is one line per kernel finding followed by `verdict <watertight|open|non-manifold|misoriented>`. Edge counts exclude edges that collapse to a point, so V - E + F - (inner loops) is the Euler characteristic. An interference result states the overlap by kind and volume; the shape output is absent when the solids do not overlap. Outputs match to `tolerance` (absolute, relative above magnitude one); the oracle recomputes them from triangle meshes with manifold-3d and three to `oracleTolerance`.",
  "tolerance": 0.000001,
  "oracleTolerance": 0.000001,
